TASK: build ONE bulletin with exactly TWO sections:
  Prefer stories confirmed by other outlets ("+N outlets"); use single-source stories only if from an official/major source.
  Use ONLY facts written in the candidate line: never add numbers, names or dates from memory.
  1. "national": {{ national }} DIFFERENT Indian stories (national politics, government, states, economy,
     markets, sports, science/space, defence, weather, education, railways, courts…), biggest first.
  2. "international": {{ international }} DIFFERENT world stories (world leaders, wars/diplomacy, global economy,
     disasters, tech giants, world sports), biggest first.
Pick the stories that most outlets are running today (trending). No two stories about the same event.
Skip gore, crime/murder/rape, family disputes, gossip, astrology, rumours, health tips and opinion pieces.

STORY RULES (very important):
- NEVER say a topic label like "खेल में", "स्वास्थ्य:", "राजनीति में", "रक्षा मोर्चे पर". Just say the news.
- Each story is ONE complete, meaningful sentence of 7–10 Hindi words: WHO did WHAT + the key detail/effect.
  Good: "पीएम मोदी ने बिहार में 12 हज़ार करोड़ की परियोजनाएं शुरू कीं।"
  Good: "RBI ने रेपो रेट 5.5% पर बरकरार रखा, EMI नहीं बदलेगी।"
  Bad (meaningless): "शेयर बाज़ार में हलचल।"  Bad (label): "खेल में, भारत जीता।"
- Split each story into "parts" so the picture changes exactly with the words:
  * 7–8 words → 1 or 2 parts; 9–10 words → 2 parts. Each part = 3–6 spoken words.
  * Each part has:
      "say":    the spoken words (Devanagari; ISRO, RBI, IPL, GDP in English letters OK; numbers as spoken)
      "visual": one English sentence: exactly what should be on screen WHILE these words are spoken
                (the real person/place/object of THIS story, Indian setting for Indian news)
      "entity": exact English Wikipedia title ONLY for a real specific person/organisation/place/vehicle
                ("Narendra Modi", "Reserve Bank of India", "Donald Trump", "Vande Bharat Express"), else ""
      "search": 2–4 English stock-photo words ("indian railway station crowd")
      "source": "entity" | "stock" | "ai"
- "on_screen_text": 2–4 Hindi words headline chip for the story.
- "src": the candidate number [n].

ALSO WRITE:
- "hook": 5–8 Hindi words, energetic, e.g. "देखिए आज की {{ count }} बड़ी खबरें, फटाफट!"
- "title": Hindi YouTube title under 70 characters naming the 2–3 biggest stories.

TOTAL spoken words (hook + all parts) must be {{ min_words }}–{{ max_words }} (about {{ seconds }} seconds).

